*BIOCHAR FEEDSTOCK PROPERTIES
! DSSAT v4.8; 03/2026
!
! Properties used by the BIOCHAR soil module to parameterise the
! two-pool decomposition model and water-retention effect.
!
! Fields:
!  CODE    5-char feedstock code used in the *BIOCHAR section of FILEX
!  CF_DM   Carbon fraction of dry mass (g C / g DM)
!  FLABIL  Labile fraction of total biochar C (fast-decomposing pool)
!  CN_DEF  Default C:N ratio if not supplied in FILEX (use 0 to require user)
!  DESCRIPTION
!
! Scientific basis:
!  CF_DM   : Mukherjee & Lal (2013), Lehmann & Joseph (2015)
!  FLABIL  : Zimmerman (2010) -- labile fraction ~5-15% depending on
!            feedstock; higher for manure/green waste, lower for wood.
!  CN_DEF  : Typical ranges from Spokas et al. (2012)
!
@CODE  CF_DM  FLABIL  CN_DEF  DESCRIPTION
WOOD   0.750  0.050    400.0  Wood biochar (hardwood, high temp)
SOFWD  0.700  0.070    300.0  Softwood biochar
STRAW  0.650  0.090    200.0  Crop straw biochar (wheat, rice)
CROP   0.650  0.080    200.0  Generic crop residue biochar
MANUR  0.550  0.130     50.0  Manure-derived biochar
GREEN  0.600  0.110     80.0  Green waste / compost biochar
SEWAG  0.520  0.150     30.0  Sewage sludge biochar
DFLT   0.600  0.080    200.0  Default biochar (use when CODE unknown)
